(902851, 101995, 25464, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous.</td>', 'Gorgeous.', '2004-09-10 01:20:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(902853, 103220, 25464, '<td valign="top">Top 10.</td>', 'Top 10.', '2004-09-10 01:20:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(902854, 103012, 25464, '<td valign="top">Interesting.  Would have looked the tiniest bit cleaner if the greenery had been edited away from the white of the spoon handle.  Good job.</td>', 'Interesting.  Would have looked the tiniest bit cleaner if the greenery had been edited away from the white of the spoon handle.  Good job.', '2004-09-10 01:22:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(902855, 102653, 10263, '<td valign="top">Its a beautiful area. Its a bit dark for my taste and seems to have  too much contrast. Love the clouds</td>', 'Its a beautiful area. Its a bit dark for my taste and seems to have  too much contrast. Love the clouds', '2004-09-10 01:27:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(902858, 103164, 22686, '<td valign="top">This seems like 2 pictures, with the foreground disconnected from the remainder. I think this is partly because the lower 3rd line runs almost exactly along that straight line parapet across your picture and also because the building and sky are so much brighter than the foreground portions. I think if I''d taken this picture I''d have lowered my POV some and tried to take in some more of the grass in the foreground and less of the sky. This would have put the lower 1/3 line as the far bank with the couples heads breaking through it to join the features together. That would also make the top 1/3 dome and sky instead of just sky so there isn''t that huge expanse of white.</td>', 'This seems like 2 pictures, with the foreground disconnected from the remainder. I think this is partly because the lower 3rd line runs almost exactly along that straight line parapet across your picture and also because the building and sky are so much brighter than the foreground portions. I think if I''d taken this picture I''d have lowered my POV some and tried to take in some more of the grass in the foreground and less of the sky. This would have put the lower 1/3 line as the far bank with the couples heads breaking through it to join the features together. That would also make the top 1/3 dome and sky instead of just sky so there isn''t that huge expanse of white.', '2004-09-10 01:29:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(902863, 102117, 22686, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful picture and a work of art in its own right - but I just can''t bring myself to think of it as a photograph.<br/> <br/>A solid 8 anyway - which is the highest I''ve given so far.</td>', 'This is a beautiful picture and a work of art in its own right - but I just can''t bring myself to think of it as a photograph. A solid 8 anyway - which is the highest I''ve given so far.', '2004-09-10 01:35:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(902867, 103223, 22686, '<td valign="top">I like this picture almost despite itself. Many photographers would have taken some effort to slow down the camera and get a silky effect on the moving water - but to me this looks better; it showes the grandeur and power of the falls instead of trying to make it looks soft.</td>', 'I like this picture almost despite itself. Many photographers would have taken some effort to slow down the camera and get a silky effect on the moving water - but to me this looks better; it showes the grandeur and power of the falls instead of trying to make it looks soft.', '2004-09-10 01:41:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(902868, 103052, 22686, '<td valign="top">Nice picture. If the foreground figure''s hat hadn''t camouflaged him amongst the stones it would have be the only 9 I gave. Still a solid 8.</td>', 'Nice picture. If the foreground figure''s hat hadn''t camouflaged him amongst the stones it would have be the only 9 I gave. Still a solid 8.', '2004-09-10 01:43:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(902886, 103224, 26660, '<td valign="top">awesome color and perspective!</td>', 'awesome color and perspective!', '2004-09-10 02:01:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(902888, 103086, 26660, '<td valign="top">awesome lighting here. great shot of sunset.</td>', 'awesome lighting here. great shot of sunset.', '2004-09-10 02:02:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(902896, 103053, 22392, '<td valign="top">great colors and the shoes are a wonderful detail. This picture makes me want to dive in immediately.</td>', 'great colors and the shoes are a wonderful detail. This picture makes me want to dive in immediately.', '2004-09-10 02:21:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(902897, 102741, 23338, '<td valign="top">... and Hoogendyks?  Love the image.  Much more romantic and nicer than those sterile old white electric generating windmills you see in California.  The highlights almost look like they are lit up with special lighting.  Thanks for the image.  Good luck with it in the challenge.</td>', '... and Hoogendyks?  Love the image.  Much more romantic and nicer than those sterile old white electric generating windmills you see in California.  The highlights almost look like they are lit up with special lighting.  Thanks for the image.  Good luck with it in the challenge.', '2004-09-10 02:21:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(902903, 102812, 23338, '<td valign="top">Cool rays.  Creates a really need mood as a photo, but I''d love to see a tad more light on some of the foreground subjects, even the closer hills.  Would just seem to make it more inviting, rather than just pretty.  Guess that''s a feeling that''s hard to put into words.  You need to "see" what is to "attract" you.  Anyway, it''s only 5% of the impact of the image regardless.  So... go with what you have.  I may be totally wrong in my opinion.  Good luck with it.</td>', 'Cool rays.  Creates a really need mood as a photo, but I''d love to see a tad more light on some of the foreground subjects, even the closer hills.  Would just seem to make it more inviting, rather than just pretty.  Guess that''s a feeling that''s hard to put into words.  You need to "see" what is to "attract" you.  Anyway, it''s only 5% of the impact of the image regardless.  So... go with what you have.  I may be totally wrong in my opinion.  Good luck with it.', '2004-09-10 02:28:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(902909, 103232, 23338, '<td valign="top">Really nice image.  Too bad it can''t be in "Backlighting" also.  Good luck with it in the challenge.</td>', 'Really nice image.  Too bad it can''t be in "Backlighting" also.  Good luck with it in the challenge.', '2004-09-10 02:31:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(902941, 103226, 19952, '<td valign="top">Having grown up in New Orleans, I have a natural affinity for shots like this. ;-) For some reason, though it seems to be a bright day, the colors came out a little bit bland. You might want to increase contrast a bit in curves or just play with the saturation to see if the blues and reds can come out looking a bit more like they really did that day. Still, this is a nicely composed shot and I think the white matte adds a nice touch.</td>', 'Having grown up in New Orleans, I have a natural affinity for shots like this. ;-) For some reason, though it seems to be a bright day, the colors came out a little bit bland. You might want to increase contrast a bit in curves or just play with the saturation to see if the blues and reds can come out looking a bit more like they really did that day. Still, this is a nicely composed shot and I think the white matte adds a nice touch.', '2004-09-10 03:29:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(902970, 101772, 6999, '<td valign="top">Quite like this composition, although I find the shot from further along toward the Eye is an easier one - the bridge and St. Stephen''s Tower organise themselves more happily.  Also like the quality in the shot - the graininess adds wonderfully to the stone textures, despite the probably out of place (for this challenge) effect in the sky. It doesn''t have the feel that I would expect from a guide book - most seem to prefer big bright clean images - but there''s a lot to like here.</td>', 'Quite like this composition, although I find the shot from further along toward the Eye is an easier one - the bridge and St. Stephen''s Tower organise themselves more happily.  Also like the quality in the shot - the graininess adds wonderfully to the stone textures, despite the probably out of place (for this challenge) effect in the sky. It doesn''t have the feel that I would expect from a guide book - most seem to prefer big bright clean images - but there''s a lot to like here.', '2004-09-10 04:48:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(902972, 102797, 6999, '<td valign="top">Good work - thugh a touch more care with the precision of your cmoposition would pay off, especially in such a regular geometric organisation. The burnt-out clouds could have been prevented by under-exposing a touch, and bringing the rest of the image back in processing. Centring the vanishing point in the frame is a bit weak - I would personally have moved it either toward the top or bottom of frame some ... probably the top, given the subject and challenge.</td>', 'Good work - thugh a touch more care with the precision of your cmoposition would pay off, especially in such a regular geometric organisation. The burnt-out clouds could have been prevented by under-exposing a touch, and bringing the rest of the image back in processing. Centring the vanishing point in the frame is a bit weak - I would personally have moved it either toward the top or bottom of frame some ... probably the top, given the subject and challenge.', '2004-09-10 04:51:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(902974, 102285, 6999, '<td valign="top">Bottom right - weird cloning artefacts? Great technical detailing, enough sense of place to suit challenge, just perhaps lacking real ping - some foreground element might help, give a sense of depth to the image? But very very clean photography, apart from the poor cloning thing.</td>', 'Bottom right - weird cloning artefacts? Great technical detailing, enough sense of place to suit challenge, just perhaps lacking real ping - some foreground element might help, give a sense of depth to the image? But very very clean photography, apart from the poor cloning thing.', '2004-09-10 04:55:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(902989, 102295, 4517, '<td valign="top">I like it but don`t fell it belongs at DPC as it is digital art.</td>', 'I like it but don`t fell it belongs at DPC as it is digital art.', '2004-09-10 05:34:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(903026, 102677, 16004, '<td valign="top">i like this quite a lot, but one thing i might gently suggest is to try cropping it say 10mm below the horizon on the water.  it''s just that the footpath is too messy with too much going on, and detracts from the simple beauty of the sculpture, the sky and the very impressive rainbow.  i love the colours (especially the green against the grey) and i hope this does well.  8.</td>', 'i like this quite a lot, but one thing i might gently suggest is to try cropping it say 10mm below the horizon on the water.  it''s just that the footpath is too messy with too much going on, and detracts from the simple beauty of the sculpture, the sky and the very impressive rainbow.  i love the colours (especially the green against the grey) and i hope this does well.  8.', '2004-09-10 07:12:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(903030, 101818, 16004, '<td valign="top">this really fits the challenge as it looks exactly like a postcard - one of the few occassions where a border really compliments and improves the purpose of a shot.  aesthetically, it''s not exactly a beautiful shot, and consequently in terms of competition might not do that well.  but i think it''s unfaultable, original, and so different from the usual icelandic church thing going on.  10.</td>', 'this really fits the challenge as it looks exactly like a postcard - one of the few occassions where a border really compliments and improves the purpose of a shot.  aesthetically, it''s not exactly a beautiful shot, and consequently in terms of competition might not do that well.  but i think it''s unfaultable, original, and so different from the usual icelandic church thing going on.  10.', '2004-09-10 07:15:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(903035, 103203, 16004, '<td valign="top">winner!  going to win.  totally briliiant - text book stuff really; beautiful water, beautiful sky, beautiful, erm, beauty.  being REALLY picky, but i might have cloned out the little white pole in the water, but that''s the only comment i can think of.  you know, i haven''t been on holiday yet this year (well, quick city break, but i was ill so that doesn''t count).  this is so far the only picture so far that makes me REALLY want to get away, so in terms of the challenge, i t succeeds in my book on all counts.  10.</td>', 'winner!  going to win.  totally briliiant - text book stuff really; beautiful water, beautiful sky, beautiful, erm, beauty.  being REALLY picky, but i might have cloned out the little white pole in the water, but that''s the only comment i can think of.  you know, i haven''t been on holiday yet this year (well, quick city break, but i was ill so that doesn''t count).  this is so far the only picture so far that makes me REALLY want to get away, so in terms of the challenge, i t succeeds in my book on all counts.  10.', '2004-09-10 07:22:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(903037, 102979, 16004, '<td valign="top">it''s a lovely shot, no question.  the colours seem a little bit washed out though.  don''t know if the contrast wants upping or what (i''m not remotely technically minded) but for me, i don''t know, i think the greens don''t look green enough.  mountains are captured well though, and looks especially majestic.  8.</td>', 'it''s a lovely shot, no question.  the colours seem a little bit washed out though.  don''t know if the contrast wants upping or what (i''m not remotely technically minded) but for me, i don''t know, i think the greens don''t look green enough.  mountains are captured well though, and looks especially majestic.  8.', '2004-09-10 07:24:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(903040, 102161, 16004, '<td valign="top">great skyline shot - it''s just a pity you''re limited to 640 pixels... very tourist guide friendly picture, so certainly fits the challenge. 8.</td>', 'great skyline shot - it''s just a pity you''re limited to 640 pixels... very tourist guide friendly picture, so certainly fits the challenge. 8.', '2004-09-10 07:38:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(903042, 102295, 16004, '<td valign="top">okay, i won''t hide the fact that i normally hate this sort of thing, i''ve never been able to see the point of why software such as PSP and PS even includes such gimmickly things for surely they have no real artistic use.  then you go ahead an do this - it''s brilliant!  the slash of green does look a little strange, can''t quite explain why (shape? angle?  not sure) but that aside i think this works brilliantly.  it''s more painting than photo, and will probably get knocked down a few places from what i think it warrants as a result.  but i think it''s superb, and has inspired me to have another play with those filters i thought 20 minutes ago were stupid.  fantastic - 10.</td>', 'okay, i won''t hide the fact that i normally hate this sort of thing, i''ve never been able to see the point of why software such as PSP and PS even includes such gimmickly things for surely they have no real artistic use.  then you go ahead an do this - it''s brilliant!  the slash of green does look a little strange, can''t quite explain why (shape? angle?  not sure) but that aside i think this works brilliantly.  it''s more painting than photo, and will probably get knocked down a few places from what i think it warrants as a result.  but i think it''s superb, and has inspired me to have another play with those filters i thought 20 minutes ago were stupid.  fantastic - 10.', '2004-09-10 07:41:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(903048, 103212, 19952, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful subject to photograph, but I think the shot came out a bit dark. That''s hard to fix under basic editing rules since the light parts of shot are already bright enough, but you can play with the dark areas when the challenge is over. For this challenge, maybe a little lightening would help and a tighter crop would cut out some of the dark sections. Hope you enjoyed your trip! :-)</td>', 'This is a beautiful subject to photograph, but I think the shot came out a bit dark. That''s hard to fix under basic editing rules since the light parts of shot are already bright enough, but you can play with the dark areas when the challenge is over. For this challenge, maybe a little lightening would help and a tighter crop would cut out some of the dark sections. Hope you enjoyed your trip! :-)', '2004-09-10 07:54:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(903050, 103217, 19952, '<td valign="top">This looks like it was a fun trip! I usually avoid noontime shots, but I think that might have been a better time for this photo since the shadows are so dark. I also think this shot might benefit from a bit more contrast to really highlight the colorful striations. Still, this is a really nice photo and a great memento from your vacation. :-)</td>', 'This looks like it was a fun trip! I usually avoid noontime shots, but I think that might have been a better time for this photo since the shadows are so dark. I also think this shot might benefit from a bit more contrast to really highlight the colorful striations. Still, this is a really nice photo and a great memento from your vacation. :-)', '2004-09-10 08:00:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(903051, 101801, 6999, '<td valign="top">Wonderfully dramatic photo, excellent composition, good colours - most things about this are rather fine. Don''t know that I could see it in a travel guide. Where is it? What''s so distinctive about it as a location? But maybe ... so I don''t mark you down.</td>', 'Wonderfully dramatic photo, excellent composition, good colours - most things about this are rather fine. Don''t know that I could see it in a travel guide. Where is it? What''s so distinctive about it as a location? But maybe ... so I don''t mark you down.', '2004-09-10 08:02:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(903052, 103154, 16004, '<td valign="top">this is a superb shot.  better than most travel guides i have seen.  the colours are brilliant (they don''t look entirely natural, and i''d be interested to learn what sort of editting was involved here), and the mix of the silhouetted family and the boats on the horizon really really works.  there really is a good degree of genius in this shot.  only very slight prerefance would be to clone out some of the crowd on the peir, but that aside, brilliant and very striking.  easy 10.</td>', 'this is a superb shot.  better than most travel guides i have seen.  the colours are brilliant (they don''t look entirely natural, and i''d be interested to learn what sort of editting was involved here), and the mix of the silhouetted family and the boats on the horizon really really works.  there really is a good degree of genius in this shot.  only very slight prerefance would be to clone out some of the crowd on the peir, but that aside, brilliant and very striking.  easy 10.', '2004-09-10 08:03:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(903053, 102350, 6999, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done - all the appropriate qualities fro the type of shot. I find the blue cast of the light a touch too cold though, but that''s my only gripe. Excellent composition all round.</td>', 'Very nicely done - all the appropriate qualities fro the type of shot. I find the blue cast of the light a touch too cold though, but that''s my only gripe. Excellent composition all round.', '2004-09-10 08:06:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(903055, 103240, 19952, '<td valign="top">Nice cool tones and a beautifully composed photograph. I even like the white matte. :-) Very good job!</td>', 'Nice cool tones and a beautifully composed photograph. I even like the white matte. :-) Very good job!', '2004-09-10 08:08:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(903058, 102784, 16004, '<td valign="top">this is so oldie worldy to be a total joy!  there are so many little details to love about this - the karmann ghia makes the shot very period, the lovely cobbles on the street are exceeding, erm, lovely.  even the lamppost adds to the overall feel.  i might recommend cloning out the notice board - it''s just too boxy, ugly, grey and modern to truly fit in. also, bloody stupid comment, but you could clone one of the green bordered cream panels and put it over the frame-less border in the middle. but that''s being picky.  looks like a lovely cafe, though. 9.</td>', 'this is so oldie worldy to be a total joy!  there are so many little details to love about this - the karmann ghia makes the shot very period, the lovely cobbles on the street are exceeding, erm, lovely.  even the lamppost adds to the overall feel.  i might recommend cloning out the notice board - it''s just too boxy, ugly, grey and modern to truly fit in. also, bloody stupid comment, but you could clone one of the green bordered cream panels and put it over the frame-less border in the middle. but that''s being picky.  looks like a lovely cafe, though. 9.', '2004-09-10 08:13:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(903061, 101658, 19952, '<td valign="top">Very nice vantage point and a beautiful photo. My personal preference would be to lower the horizon a bit to put the Space Needle right on the top left third line. The only other thing I notice is that the mountain looks a bit odd, either from haze or overprocessing. Still, this is a really nice photo - one of the best in the challenge.</td>', 'Very nice vantage point and a beautiful photo. My personal preference would be to lower the horizon a bit to put the Space Needle right on the top left third line. The only other thing I notice is that the mountain looks a bit odd, either from haze or overprocessing. Still, this is a really nice photo - one of the best in the challenge.', '2004-09-10 08:15:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(903062, 102999, 16004, '<td valign="top">very brave - was this in florida?  you have certainly captured the drama, and i think the noise / graininess of the image works especially well in this case.  the burning at the sides is another nice touch.  very good shot, and splendid choice for the challenge - so few people posted shots of negative things.  9.</td>', 'very brave - was this in florida?  you have certainly captured the drama, and i think the noise / graininess of the image works especially well in this case.  the burning at the sides is another nice touch.  very good shot, and splendid choice for the challenge - so few people posted shots of negative things.  9.', '2004-09-10 08:16:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(903066, 102666, 19952, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful photo with excellent color and composition. I love the use of the black background to draw attention to the bird''s bright colors. Really nice job.</td>', 'This is a beautiful photo with excellent color and composition. I love the use of the black background to draw attention to the bird''s bright colors. Really nice job.', '2004-09-10 08:20:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(903067, 102876, 24642, '<td valign="top">I am a sucker for road shots.  This one is nice.  I would have prefered more road less sky but anyways good job.</td>', 'I am a sucker for road shots.  This one is nice.  I would have prefered more road less sky but anyways good job.', '2004-09-10 08:21:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(903068, 103247, 24642, '<td valign="top">Nice sky and clouds.  Would have liked to see more of the road though.</td>', 'Nice sky and clouds.  Would have liked to see more of the road though.', '2004-09-10 08:22:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(903069, 103064, 16004, '<td valign="top">nice picture - colours are particularly pleasant.  However, composition wise it''s a bit odd - not sure having the left portion cut off and the right side of the surface it''s resting on quite works.  also, north in the southwest position and the arrow pointing west is a bit disorientating.  i think there are certain unwritten protocols with photographing compassessess (compaii?) that have to be considered. dunno.  overall the picture is very nice, colours ARE lovely and the focus unquestionably good.  fits the challenge also.  6.</td>', 'nice picture - colours are particularly pleasant.  However, composition wise it''s a bit odd - not sure having the left portion cut off and the right side of the surface it''s resting on quite works.  also, north in the southwest position and the arrow pointing west is a bit disorientating.  i think there are certain unwritten protocols with photographing compassessess (compaii?) that have to be considered. dunno.  overall the picture is very nice, colours ARE lovely and the focus unquestionably good.  fits the challenge also.  6.', '2004-09-10 08:23:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(903071, 103065, 16004, '<td valign="top">i can only assume it''s appreciate your church week in iceland - there are loads of the buggers this week.  it''s very dramatic and gothicesque though - i think the B&amp;W works well and i love the light cast on the tower.  the sky is very ominous and powerful, though the halo around the top of the tower reduces the impact a little bit.  i wonder how it would look more landscaped in orientation though - one can''t help think that the dreaded rule-of-thirds might be a viable thing here...   it''s still very captivating though - kind of film-noir esque hammer horror type thing (half expect lightning bolts and a powerful score to accompany the picture - sequal to van helsing or similar could be filmed here).  excellent lighting.  9.</td>', 'i can only assume it''s appreciate your church week in iceland - there are loads of the buggers this week.  it''s very dramatic and gothicesque though - i think the B&W works well and i love the light cast on the tower.  the sky is very ominous and powerful, though the halo around the top of the tower reduces the impact a little bit.  i wonder how it would look more landscaped in orientation though - one can''t help think that the dreaded rule-of-thirds might be a viable thing here...   it''s still very captivating though - kind of film-noir esque hammer horror type thing (half expect lightning bolts and a powerful score to accompany the picture - sequal to van helsing or similar could be filmed here).  excellent lighting.  9.', '2004-09-10 08:29:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(903074, 103112, 22125, '<td valign="top">why the border,nice pic without it.my eye keeps going to the border, sorry 5</td>', 'why the border,nice pic without it.my eye keeps going to the border, sorry 5', '2004-09-10 08:35:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(903075, 103053, 16004, '<td valign="top">nice shot - though the umbrella would have been brilliant for this weeks open challenge.  water is very enticing, must confess - though the beach is a bit on the grey side...   6.</td>', 'nice shot - though the umbrella would have been brilliant for this weeks open challenge.  water is very enticing, must confess - though the beach is a bit on the grey side...   6.', '2004-09-10 08:37:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(903079, 103074, 22125, '<td valign="top">This is my most favioured shot of this comp, I would love to walk down that track. 10</td>', 'This is my most favioured shot of this comp, I would love to walk down that track. 10', '2004-09-10 08:48:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(903081, 102093, 531, '<td valign="top">Well, nothing''s so special but I like it.</td>', 'Well, nothing''s so special but I like it.', '2004-09-10 08:53:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(903083, 103238, 16004, '<td valign="top">I really do like this - i do so love stairs!  unfortunately the wonkiness of the shot is very distracting, and could easily be fixed with a moderate amount of rotation.  also, a bit of light in the lower left flight might have lessened the oppressive blackness in this portion.  i like the almost-sepia tones and the graininess though, and the "unknown" light at the top works very well.  6.</td>', 'I really do like this - i do so love stairs!  unfortunately the wonkiness of the shot is very distracting, and could easily be fixed with a moderate amount of rotation.  also, a bit of light in the lower left flight might have lessened the oppressive blackness in this portion.  i like the almost-sepia tones and the graininess though, and the "unknown" light at the top works very well.  6.', '2004-09-10 08:59:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(903085, 102248, 16004, '<td valign="top">what is it about iceland?  the shot isn''t even in iceland, and yet there the bleeders are!  ;)  it''s a cute shot, possibly a little on the sarcastic side (maybe it''s not the intention?) but doesn''t really say travel guide to me.  good in-joke though.  5.</td>', 'what is it about iceland?  the shot isn''t even in iceland, and yet there the bleeders are!  ;)  it''s a cute shot, possibly a little on the sarcastic side (maybe it''s not the intention?) but doesn''t really say travel guide to me.  good in-joke though.  5.', '2004-09-10 09:01:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(903090, 102808, 16004, '<td valign="top">nice arse! (well, i think it looks like a lovely ladies back and bum.  i can''t be the only one who has said this).  <br/> <br/>sky is very pleasant and interesting to look at, but then focus should be on the travel-type stuff, and a silhouette of a roof (no matter how pleasingly suggestive it might be) doesn''t really scream "put me in a travel guide".  with the architecture that is evident from this shot, i think a little less emphasis on the sky might improve your overall score.  for me, a 4.</td>', 'nice arse! (well, i think it looks like a lovely ladies back and bum.  i can''t be the only one who has said this).   sky is very pleasant and interesting to look at, but then focus should be on the travel-type stuff, and a silhouette of a roof (no matter how pleasingly suggestive it might be) doesn''t really scream "put me in a travel guide".  with the architecture that is evident from this shot, i think a little less emphasis on the sky might improve your overall score.  for me, a 4.', '2004-09-10 09:11:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(903099, 101592, 16004, '<td valign="top">winner for strangest take on the challenge?  don''t know.  erm, nice shot of the moon.  must admit in my local borders i haven''t seen many travel guides pertaining to other planetary bodies, but that''s not to say you''re not (a millenia) ahead of your time.  it''s nice and detailed, though the centred composition is a bit too in your face for my personal likings.  7.</td>', 'winner for strangest take on the challenge?  don''t know.  erm, nice shot of the moon.  must admit in my local borders i haven''t seen many travel guides pertaining to other planetary bodies, but that''s not to say you''re not (a millenia) ahead of your time.  it''s nice and detailed, though the centred composition is a bit too in your face for my personal likings.  7.', '2004-09-10 09:23:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(903125, 103209, 2764, '<td valign="top">I really hope this photo does well - its not what i would put into a travel brochure - but I really like it<br/>I like the strong lines.  I like how the people contrast with the institution in every way . Heay, light.  straight lines - human shapes.  Static and stil, a hint of movement and wind on the skirts.  The two women on the right show the most contrast and the most movement - perhaps the woman on the left who sets herself apart is half way to being turned into stone,  9</td>', 'I really hope this photo does well - its not what i would put into a travel brochure - but I really like itI like the strong lines.  I like how the people contrast with the institution in every way . Heay, light.  straight lines - human shapes.  Static and stil, a hint of movement and wind on the skirts.  The two women on the right show the most contrast and the most movement - perhaps the woman on the left who sets herself apart is half way to being turned into stone,  9', '2004-09-10 10:08:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(903254, 101995, 24454, '<td valign="top">I love this picture!  I just got back from Estes Park last week, and got some great shot of this striking Church at St. Malo, but none at this time of day, which makes it even more striking!  I love that area so much!   You certainly have lots of choices for travel pictures in that area, don''t you?   Good job!</td>', 'I love this picture!  I just got back from Estes Park last week, and got some great shot of this striking Church at St. Malo, but none at this time of day, which makes it even more striking!  I love that area so much!   You certainly have lots of choices for travel pictures in that area, don''t you?   Good job!', '2004-09-10 11:42:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(903258, 103067, 24454, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!  I want to go there!</td>', 'Beautiful!  I want to go there!', '2004-09-10 11:44:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(903262, 103223, 24454, '<td valign="top">Wow!  Way to capture that!  It DEFINITELY makes me wish I was there!</td>', 'Wow!  Way to capture that!  It DEFINITELY makes me wish I was there!', '2004-09-10 11:46:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(903266, 102666, 24454, '<td valign="top">What a great picture.  It''s so crisp, it could almost look like a painting.  I could seriously see this on a brochure!</td>', 'What a great picture.  It''s so crisp, it could almost look like a painting.  I could seriously see this on a brochure!', '2004-09-10 11:48:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(903268, 102364, 24454, '<td valign="top">Oooooooh, very beautiful capture of the inviting night scenery.  This is perfect for a travel brochure!</td>', 'Oooooooh, very beautiful capture of the inviting night scenery.  This is perfect for a travel brochure!', '2004-09-10 11:49:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(903269, 102435, 8367, '<td valign="top">Great photo, but I think I''ll pass on visiting you anytime soon. :)</td>', 'Great photo, but I think I''ll pass on visiting you anytime soon. :)', '2004-09-10 11:49:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(903271, 102816, 24454, '<td valign="top">Great depth of field.  This is crystal clear from the front to the back.  Very nice.  Perfect for a travel ad!</td>', 'Great depth of field.  This is crystal clear from the front to the back.  Very nice.  Perfect for a travel ad!', '2004-09-10 11:49:54.000000', NULL, 1),
