(908135, 101801, 15497, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC!<br/> <br/>What can I say? Simply brilliant! I wouldn''t have changed a bit in this photograph. You have captured a moment, and it''s very inspiring. Congratulations with a well deserved yellow ribbon.<br/> <br/>Terje<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the CC! What can I say? Simply brilliant! I wouldn''t have changed a bit in this photograph. You have captured a moment, and it''s very inspiring. Congratulations with a well deserved yellow ribbon. Terje ', '2004-09-13 18:29:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(908226, 103141, 6349, '<td valign="top">Sorry I was wrong.  Really thought this would have done better.  It is exceptional for the travel guide challenge.  Can''t believe I was one of only 7 tens.</td>', 'Sorry I was wrong.  Really thought this would have done better.  It is exceptional for the travel guide challenge.  Can''t believe I was one of only 7 tens.', '2004-09-13 19:21:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(908232, 103160, 6349, '<td valign="top">I can''t believe this didn''t break 6!  It was one of my favorites in the challenge.  I suppose it just wasn''t great for "travel guides"</td>', 'I can''t believe this didn''t break 6!  It was one of my favorites in the challenge.  I suppose it just wasn''t great for "travel guides"', '2004-09-13 19:25:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(908240, 102435, 6349, '<td valign="top">Just so you know, I gave this a 7 and am very confused by the scoring.</td>', 'Just so you know, I gave this a 7 and am very confused by the scoring.', '2004-09-13 19:28:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(908285, 103074, 6999, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised by the provenance of this ... the texture of the shot, the contrast, the detail, the sense of grain all seem to be your work. The green border ... (expression of horror)! I''m afraid I voted it way down, just for that: I cannot look at the image without my eye being drawn to that green square, and that makes it difficult. Where white or black serves to isolate from environment, alows you to choose the context of exhibition, this ... well, it baffles me. I''d love you to explain the thinking.<br/> <br/>E</td>', 'I''m surprised by the provenance of this ... the texture of the shot, the contrast, the detail, the sense of grain all seem to be your work. The green border ... (expression of horror)! I''m afraid I voted it way down, just for that: I cannot look at the image without my eye being drawn to that green square, and that makes it difficult. Where white or black serves to isolate from environment, alows you to choose the context of exhibition, this ... well, it baffles me. I''d love you to explain the thinking. E', '2004-09-13 19:58:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(908290, 103224, 18485, '<td valign="top">knew it was you~~great showing here rob...  i really liked this entry, perfect tone.</td>', 'knew it was you~~great showing here rob...  i really liked this entry, perfect tone.', '2004-09-13 20:03:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(908341, 103255, 2716, '<td valign="top">Bro !!! Great shot.  I have to go there some day.  Keep up the good work.</td>', 'Bro !!! Great shot.  I have to go there some day.  Keep up the good work.', '2004-09-13 21:00:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(908353, 102350, 4871, '<td valign="top">Hi everyone! Thanks for all your fantastic comments - I think I''m going to need a couple of weeks for my head to return to normal size!!<br/> <br/>I have submitted this image to DPC Prints for approval so it should be online shortly if you want to buy any prints, and I''ve made use of the fact that I can combine more than one image. I''ve taken the sky from a locked off shot of the same position with a darker exposure and when combined the sky doesn''t look quite so ''wierd'' as it does in my submission. I''ve also warmed the picture using Photoshop CS''s warming filter. I''d be interested to receive some feedback if you think its better than my submission.<br/> <br/>Once again thanks for the ribbon and for the compliments :)<br/> <br/>PS You can view other pics of our holiday to Yorkshire at <a href="https://www.pbase.com/p_johns/yorkshire" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">www.pbase.com/p_johns/yorkshire</a> where there''s some others I''m really proud of.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-09-13 20:16:36.</i></td>', 'Hi everyone! Thanks for all your fantastic comments - I think I''m going to need a couple of weeks for my head to return to normal size!! I have submitted this image to DPC Prints for approval so it should be online shortly if you want to buy any prints, and I''ve made use of the fact that I can combine more than one image. I''ve taken the sky from a locked off shot of the same position with a darker exposure and when combined the sky doesn''t look quite so ''wierd'' as it does in my submission. I''ve also warmed the picture using Photoshop CS''s warming filter. I''d be interested to receive some feedback if you think its better than my submission. Once again thanks for the ribbon and for the compliments :) PS You can view other pics of our holiday to Yorkshire at www.pbase.com/p_johns/yorkshire where there''s some others I''m really proud of.', '2004-09-13 21:15:18.000000', '2004-09-13 21:16:36.000000', 0),
(908425, 102350, 10413, '<td valign="top">Beautiful photo. Congrat6ulations on a well deserved first place.</td>', 'Beautiful photo. Congrat6ulations on a well deserved first place.', '2004-09-13 22:13:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(908444, 102350, 4877, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Phil!!!  great photo!<br/>That trip certainly paid off!<br/>Andrew</td>', 'Congratulations Phil!!!  great photo!That trip certainly paid off!Andrew', '2004-09-13 22:23:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(908460, 101801, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, this is a wonderful image! A long overdue ribbon for a talented creative photographer. Didn''t you just post somewhere that you were not planning to ribbon anytime soon? Anyway, good to see recognition of fine work.</td>', 'Congratulations, this is a wonderful image! A long overdue ribbon for a talented creative photographer. Didn''t you just post somewhere that you were not planning to ribbon anytime soon? Anyway, good to see recognition of fine work.', '2004-09-13 22:37:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(908463, 103224, 8891, '<td valign="top">Thanks, m!</td>', 'Thanks, m!', '2004-09-13 22:39:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(908466, 102350, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on Your Blue Ribbon, this is a spectacular shot!</td>', 'Congratulations on Your Blue Ribbon, this is a spectacular shot!', '2004-09-13 22:40:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(908469, 101995, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a stunning entry and your first ribbon! Well done!</td>', 'Congratulations on a stunning entry and your first ribbon! Well done!', '2004-09-13 22:43:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(908478, 102518, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on placing 4th with this amazing image.</td>', 'Congratulations on placing 4th with this amazing image.', '2004-09-13 22:51:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(908648, 103160, 11977, '<td valign="top">This photo was my favorite in the challenge and should have done much better.  Maybe you wouldn''t see it in a travel guide, but it certainly depicts NYC.  IMHO the legs in the foreground make the shot.</td>', 'This photo was my favorite in the challenge and should have done much better.  Maybe you wouldn''t see it in a travel guide, but it certainly depicts NYC.  IMHO the legs in the foreground make the shot.', '2004-09-14 00:31:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(908656, 102518, 19248, '<td valign="top">Congrats, on 4th I thought this would have ribboned.</td>', 'Congrats, on 4th I thought this would have ribboned.', '2004-09-14 00:40:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(908657, 103255, 19248, '<td valign="top">Congrats, I had this a 10.</td>', 'Congrats, I had this a 10.', '2004-09-14 00:41:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(908662, 102332, 19248, '<td valign="top">I loved this shot.  Congrats on 17th.  10 from me, adding to my favorites.</td>', 'I loved this shot.  Congrats on 17th.  10 from me, adding to my favorites.', '2004-09-14 00:44:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(908689, 101995, 20952, '<td valign="top">Great job.  You deserve the ribbon finally after so many other great shots that didn''t make it.  Keep it up.</td>', 'Great job.  You deserve the ribbon finally after so many other great shots that didn''t make it.  Keep it up.', '2004-09-14 01:10:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(908757, 103051, 8054, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by siggi:</b></div><hr/><i> Since you mention me by name in your post.<br/> <br/>Isn''t it enough to discover new locations. There poses is not helping the composition. I don''t find ithe pose fitting for a travel guide ether. I find the photo better without the girls in it.<br/>You may ask why again...<br/>When I look at the photo my eyes see a beutifull beach, then I see the girls bending over looking at something, I start to look for what they are looking for and see nothing there...  not helping the composition. Gave you 5 like most.<br/>Would like this picture more without the girls there.<br/> <br/>ps.<br/>Looked over the other comments, the once that are commenting on what might make this picture better you dont chekck the "Photographer found comment helpful" box, and we are only trying to help. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I guess I just disagree with you in general not to say that I am right and you are wrong and vice versa. I just had a different vision when editing this photo for the challenge and we happen to disagree. It''s normal.<br/> <br/>As for not checking your comments as helpful, my only reason for not checking them is because I disagree with the opinions contained within. As you can see from my other challenge entries, I usually check off many of them as different people provide different insight to my photos. Then there are the people that do not check off a single comment as useful. They must be 100% right all of the time and always take perfect photos and do not want to be bothered by comments even those that compliment the photo. I try to have an open mind when reading the comments. Also I did agree with ellamay about the people pointing out of frame so I do find comments helpful, even the ones I find negative.<br/> <br/><b>More stuff:</b> <br/> <br/>Siggi,<br/> <br/>I am not trying to pick a fight with you personally. I just want to make that clear. I respect you and your work and just wanted to have a constructive agrument between two people who love photography. If I gave you any other impression, I apologize.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-09-14 01:38:57.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by siggi: Since you mention me by name in your post. Isn''t it enough to discover new locations. There poses is not helping the composition. I don''t find ithe pose fitting for a travel guide ether. I find the photo better without the girls in it.You may ask why again...When I look at the photo my eyes see a beutifull beach, then I see the girls bending over looking at something, I start to look for what they are looking for and see nothing there...  not helping the composition. Gave you 5 like most.Would like this picture more without the girls there. ps.Looked over the other comments, the once that are commenting on what might make this picture better you dont chekck the "Photographer found comment helpful" box, and we are only trying to help.   I guess I just disagree with you in general not to say that I am right and you are wrong and vice versa. I just had a different vision when editing this photo for the challenge and we happen to disagree. It''s normal. As for not checking your comments as helpful, my only reason for not checking them is because I disagree with the opinions contained within. As you can see from my other challenge entries, I usually check off many of them as different people provide different insight to my photos. Then there are the people that do not check off a single comment as useful. They must be 100% right all of the time and always take perfect photos and do not want to be bothered by comments even those that compliment the photo. I try to have an open mind when reading the comments. Also I did agree with ellamay about the people pointing out of frame so I do find comments helpful, even the ones I find negative. More stuff:  Siggi, I am not trying to pick a fight with you personally. I just want to make that clear. I respect you and your work and just wanted to have a constructive agrument between two people who love photography. If I gave you any other impression, I apologize.', '2004-09-14 02:30:33.000000', '2004-09-14 02:38:57.000000', 0),
