(911646, 103188, 16266, '<td valign="top">interesting shot, and nice landscape.  The colors could be a little more vibrant.  There doesn''t seem to be much for darks in the image.  I think it is a cool image with the parasailer there, but he is so very small that it isn''t part of the main subject of the photo.  i had to look at the photo for a while before i saw him.  Perhaps it feels a bit akwardly cropped, but i understand why you did that, or assume that you did that to get the parasailer  in the image, large enough, yet including the mountains.<br/>So overall, good image, parasailer too small, akward crop.<br/>-from the critique club.</td>', 'interesting shot, and nice landscape.  The colors could be a little more vibrant.  There doesn''t seem to be much for darks in the image.  I think it is a cool image with the parasailer there, but he is so very small that it isn''t part of the main subject of the photo.  i had to look at the photo for a while before i saw him.  Perhaps it feels a bit akwardly cropped, but i understand why you did that, or assume that you did that to get the parasailer  in the image, large enough, yet including the mountains.So overall, good image, parasailer too small, akward crop.-from the critique club.', '2004-09-15 15:31:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(911746, 102350, 9441, '<td valign="top">What a magnificient piece of work!  Great job on this.  Definitely deserving of the blue!  Congrats on a job well done!</td>', 'What a magnificient piece of work!  Great job on this.  Definitely deserving of the blue!  Congrats on a job well done!', '2004-09-15 16:39:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(911756, 103188, 1031, '<td valign="top">: ) I found the parasailer easily enough, mostly because (based on the thumbnail view) I was looking to see which end of those contrails the planes were at.<br/> <br/>I think I might agree with <b>leaf</b> that it could be cropped a little top and bottom (I''d crop to a 3:2 ratio) without losing anything critical; perhaps the river disappearing in the trees in the lower-left. I think that''s compensated-for by puting the parasailer (title subject) real close to the top edge. That makes it easier to spot, and it''s a goodway to isolate and add visual strength and importance to a small subject (c.f. <a href="//dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=5783" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Cowspace</a> by Remie for the example which came to mind).</td>', ': ) I found the parasailer easily enough, mostly because (based on the thumbnail view) I was looking to see which end of those contrails the planes were at. I think I might agree with leaf that it could be cropped a little top and bottom (I''d crop to a 3:2 ratio) without losing anything critical; perhaps the river disappearing in the trees in the lower-left. I think that''s compensated-for by puting the parasailer (title subject) real close to the top edge. That makes it easier to spot, and it''s a goodway to isolate and add visual strength and importance to a small subject (c.f. Cowspace by Remie for the example which came to mind).', '2004-09-15 16:46:43.000000', NULL, 0),
