(913376, 103224, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Banmorn...<br/> <br/>This is an excellent urban architectural photo.  I must also add that you did an excellent job with your perspective correction in this photo.  Most people don''t take that little extra effort and it makes a huge difference in the results :)  Reading your notes, I''m also impressed that you shot this scene over a period of two days in an effort to find the best possible time/conditions for the image.  This type of effort is often what it takes to make a successful photo.  I see tons of images here on DPChallenge that have potential, but just don''t succeed because the photographer didn''t take the time and effort to make it work as you have here.  <br/> <br/>This composition just works nicely.  The two buildings on the sides nicely frame the architecture of the center building and help bring the viewer right to that point.  <br/> <br/>Excellent work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Banmorn... This is an excellent urban architectural photo.  I must also add that you did an excellent job with your perspective correction in this photo.  Most people don''t take that little extra effort and it makes a huge difference in the results :)  Reading your notes, I''m also impressed that you shot this scene over a period of two days in an effort to find the best possible time/conditions for the image.  This type of effort is often what it takes to make a successful photo.  I see tons of images here on DPChallenge that have potential, but just don''t succeed because the photographer didn''t take the time and effort to make it work as you have here.   This composition just works nicely.  The two buildings on the sides nicely frame the architecture of the center building and help bring the viewer right to that point.   Excellent work :) John Setzler', '2004-09-16 17:23:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(913467, 102350, 22781, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club Comment:</b> <br/> <br/>How could I ever Critique this?<br/>This is a wonderfull almost unreal photo, the lights, the trees, the smoke, the reflection of the water all add to the picture.<br/>What I personaly like is the church in the background, it gives it more depth.<br/>What''s another great thing about this one is that you can come back to it as much as you like and just find another overlooked detail, search for something new every time, it''s just as taking a little trip :)<br/> <br/>Now for some Critique, what could have been done to improve this picture? You gave the answer yourself, the sky is a bit boring, and it has a un-natural color, maybe because of post processing, but i''m glad you didn''t crop tighter, if you ever buy the ND filter and if you go back there ....... :)<br/> <br/>There was a lot to do about the border, personaly I don''t care about the border here, it doesn''t take anything away from the photo, but the photo can stand on it''s own, so it doesn''t need a border.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your blue, it''s a deserved one!</td>', 'Critique Club Comment:  How could I ever Critique this?This is a wonderfull almost unreal photo, the lights, the trees, the smoke, the reflection of the water all add to the picture.What I personaly like is the church in the background, it gives it more depth.What''s another great thing about this one is that you can come back to it as much as you like and just find another overlooked detail, search for something new every time, it''s just as taking a little trip :) Now for some Critique, what could have been done to improve this picture? You gave the answer yourself, the sky is a bit boring, and it has a un-natural color, maybe because of post processing, but i''m glad you didn''t crop tighter, if you ever buy the ND filter and if you go back there ....... :) There was a lot to do about the border, personaly I don''t care about the border here, it doesn''t take anything away from the photo, but the photo can stand on it''s own, so it doesn''t need a border. Congratulations on your blue, it''s a deserved one!', '2004-09-16 18:35:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(913828, 102124, 24896, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by thatcloudthere:</b></div><hr/><i> Holy crap!<br/> <br/>I would never ever have guessed that this would end up 1 away from a brown ribbon! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Same here! I thought this pic was good not great...but defiantly not second to last.  I really liked the composition. The pic was framed really well. I gave it a 6 I don''t post my scores often but this is a pic that voting went astray on.  I really like the spot of light coming through the silo and the sky adds great mood.  It could have used a little more exposure or some curves.  Its not the best DOF but works well with this pic. You did get a comment from graphicfunk so do consider it a good pic.  I have learned a lot from comments on this site and I find graphicfunk''s some of the best.<br/> <br/>edit-spelling<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-09-16 22:04:41.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by thatcloudthere: Holy crap! I would never ever have guessed that this would end up 1 away from a brown ribbon!   Same here! I thought this pic was good not great...but defiantly not second to last.  I really liked the composition. The pic was framed really well. I gave it a 6 I don''t post my scores often but this is a pic that voting went astray on.  I really like the spot of light coming through the silo and the sky adds great mood.  It could have used a little more exposure or some curves.  Its not the best DOF but works well with this pic. You did get a comment from graphicfunk so do consider it a good pic.  I have learned a lot from comments on this site and I find graphicfunk''s some of the best. edit-spelling', '2004-09-16 23:03:03.000000', '2004-09-16 23:04:41.000000', 0),
