(914243, 102694, 22781, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club Comment:</b> <br/> <br/>Your highest scoring photo until now, and almost hit the big 6! You must be pleased.<br/>Now its my task to critique you. Lets see.<br/> <br/>This was a very difficult challenge, as far as Im concerned, with lots of beautiful pictures and this is one of them.<br/> <br/>What do I like about this photo:<br/>It has a really nice nostalgic look,  and I personally like old cars. The composition is good.<br/>I could see this in a travel guide, but its not as obvious as other pics in this challenge.<br/>The b&amp;w conversion works for this photo.<br/> <br/>Now for some critique:<br/>What could have been done to improve this? Well for once the building in the background is blown out, so it takes away from the picture, the highlights, shadows and reflections on the car are also a bit distracting in my eyes, I dont know how the whole place looks, but maybe you could have used a different point of view to compose it different. I would like to see a picture from the other side with the gas station, and see what that would bring.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Comment:  Your highest scoring photo until now, and almost hit the big 6! You must be pleased.Now its my task to critique you. Lets see. This was a very difficult challenge, as far as Im concerned, with lots of beautiful pictures and this is one of them. What do I like about this photo:It has a really nice nostalgic look,  and I personally like old cars. The composition is good.I could see this in a travel guide, but its not as obvious as other pics in this challenge.The b&w conversion works for this photo. Now for some critique:What could have been done to improve this? Well for once the building in the background is blown out, so it takes away from the picture, the highlights, shadows and reflections on the car are also a bit distracting in my eyes, I dont know how the whole place looks, but maybe you could have used a different point of view to compose it different. I would like to see a picture from the other side with the gas station, and see what that would bring.', '2004-09-17 06:14:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(914655, 103042, 22781, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club Comment:</b> <br/> <br/>A very nice photo to look at, I always like balloons.<br/>I like the POV youve chosen to take this picture, it looks like you are high up yourself, maybe even in a balloon.<br/>Personally, I scored you a bit higher then you finished, and I was thinking that this would be at least a top 50 score, well you know how it is by now, you cant predict the voters.<br/> <br/>Now for some critique:<br/> <br/>Lighting: Because of the very bright sky the balloons are almost silhouettes, if you had been with your back to the sun the real subject of your photo, the balloons, would be better lighted. As you know, many voters dont ajust their monitors and they will only see black balloons, I personally think that you lost some points because of that.<br/> <br/>Composition: Now as Im staring at this picture longer, I notice that there is not 1 real object to look at, its a bit busy. Like Ismart already said, if you had 1 big balloon on the foreground, and the smaller ones on the background, this would give some rest. It would also put some more depth in the photo.<br/> <br/>About the odd-shaped (pac-man) balloon, hey, its a balloon and it has all the right to be there, thats just the way it is.<br/> <br/>Then just one more point where I think you might have lost points, travel guide, I think some people wont believe that this would be in a travel guide. I can tell you (I mean the voters) this kind of photos IS in travel guides. <br/> <br/>Well, all in all I still like this photo and I hope you still like it too.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or just want to chat :-) just PM me<br/> <br/>Grrrtzzz<br/> <br/>Peter<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Comment:  A very nice photo to look at, I always like balloons.I like the POV youve chosen to take this picture, it looks like you are high up yourself, maybe even in a balloon.Personally, I scored you a bit higher then you finished, and I was thinking that this would be at least a top 50 score, well you know how it is by now, you cant predict the voters. Now for some critique: Lighting: Because of the very bright sky the balloons are almost silhouettes, if you had been with your back to the sun the real subject of your photo, the balloons, would be better lighted. As you know, many voters dont ajust their monitors and they will only see black balloons, I personally think that you lost some points because of that. Composition: Now as Im staring at this picture longer, I notice that there is not 1 real object to look at, its a bit busy. Like Ismart already said, if you had 1 big balloon on the foreground, and the smaller ones on the background, this would give some rest. It would also put some more depth in the photo. About the odd-shaped (pac-man) balloon, hey, its a balloon and it has all the right to be there, thats just the way it is. Then just one more point where I think you might have lost points, travel guide, I think some people wont believe that this would be in a travel guide. I can tell you (I mean the voters) this kind of photos IS in travel guides.  Well, all in all I still like this photo and I hope you still like it too. If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or just want to chat :-) just PM me Grrrtzzz Peter', '2004-09-17 15:54:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(914739, 101611, 22781, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club Comment:</b> <br/> <br/>I am looking at a technically great picture, guess what, its yours!<br/>Lighting: Spot on. 100%<br/>Composition: Great, a very interesting image.<br/>Color and sharpness: fine.<br/>I really like this photo, like the sky, the clouds the color of the wood against the sky, but why did you score so low? (I took a look at your profile and have seen ribbon winning pics)<br/> <br/>Well I can only guess:  The voters didnt get what you where trying to say.<br/>Keep in mind that voting a photo generally only takes seconds. Most voters expect something, and when they dont get what they want they vote low.<br/>So the question is, does this meet the challenge? I would have to say yes. But not a big yes.<br/>If you take a look at the photos higher up (lets say top 20) youll see that most of them have composed their shot with something recognizable about the country/city that they presented, some of them (mine) are not even good pictures, but are scoring high just for being simple, voters know what it is they are looking at.<br/> <br/>I guess you wanted to do something different, and didnt get the appreciation you expected.<br/>Keep in mind that not all voters vote because of the same thing. Some vote high on photos they like and low on photos they dont like. Some others vote low if they think you dont meet the challenge and others vote low on every flower, cat, dog or child.<br/> <br/>Keep it simple, let your message get trough without thinking.<br/> <br/>That said I just want to say again that this picture (without thinking of the challenge) is very attractive and well composed, nive POV, nice DOF all add to this interesting photo. Nice work. <br/> <br/>If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me. <br/> <br/>Grrrtzzz <br/> <br/>Peter<br/> <br/>PS: I scored you much higher then your final score.<br/> <br/>Editted because of typo...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-09-17 16:20:16.</i></td>', 'Critique Club Comment:  I am looking at a technically great picture, guess what, its yours!Lighting: Spot on. 100%Composition: Great, a very interesting image.Color and sharpness: fine.I really like this photo, like the sky, the clouds the color of the wood against the sky, but why did you score so low? (I took a look at your profile and have seen ribbon winning pics) Well I can only guess:  The voters didnt get what you where trying to say.Keep in mind that voting a photo generally only takes seconds. Most voters expect something, and when they dont get what they want they vote low.So the question is, does this meet the challenge? I would have to say yes. But not a big yes.If you take a look at the photos higher up (lets say top 20) youll see that most of them have composed their shot with something recognizable about the country/city that they presented, some of them (mine) are not even good pictures, but are scoring high just for being simple, voters know what it is they are looking at. I guess you wanted to do something different, and didnt get the appreciation you expected.Keep in mind that not all voters vote because of the same thing. Some vote high on photos they like and low on photos they dont like. Some others vote low if they think you dont meet the challenge and others vote low on every flower, cat, dog or child. Keep it simple, let your message get trough without thinking. That said I just want to say again that this picture (without thinking of the challenge) is very attractive and well composed, nive POV, nice DOF all add to this interesting photo. Nice work.  If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me.  Grrrtzzz  Peter PS: I scored you much higher then your final score. Editted because of typo...', '2004-09-17 17:15:50.000000', '2004-09-17 17:20:16.000000', 0),
(914785, 101884, 22781, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club Comment:</b> <br/> <br/>Indeed, I agree with most of the comments below, and let me take this time to congratulate you on a 6+ score on your 2nd challenge.<br/>The big 6 (as I call it) is not easy to reach imho, and says something about your photo.<br/>The color of the flamingo is absolutely amazing, and the detail and sharpness (as I understand you didnt even use USM) is brilliant. <br/>Just let me say that this is realy a pretty picture, and I guess it would look good framed, hanging on somebodys wall (hint, hint)<br/> <br/>Now about some critique:<br/> <br/>Yes there are still some things to say about this picture.<br/>Title: I dont think the title adds something to this photo. I am to lazy to come up with something better now, but its long and doeas not realy tell you anything more.<br/> <br/>Composition: Good, you didnt crop, this is what came out of your camera, but maybe, just maybe with a little wider shot, this could be even better. I guess you tried that, and you have lots of pictures of this same bird on your hard disk, and this was the best one, but I would still like to see just  a bit more maybe<br/> <br/>As you already said yourself, the other flamingo could have been cloned out, and it would have made the beautiful contrast with the black background even more perfect, but I dont find it really distracting.<br/> <br/>Again, its a beautiful picture, and if I where you I would put it up for print, or at least hang it on your own wall.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me. <br/> <br/>Grrrtzzz <br/> <br/>Peter<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-09-17 16:48:09.</i></td>', 'Critique Club Comment:  Indeed, I agree with most of the comments below, and let me take this time to congratulate you on a 6+ score on your 2nd challenge.The big 6 (as I call it) is not easy to reach imho, and says something about your photo.The color of the flamingo is absolutely amazing, and the detail and sharpness (as I understand you didnt even use USM) is brilliant. Just let me say that this is realy a pretty picture, and I guess it would look good framed, hanging on somebodys wall (hint, hint) Now about some critique: Yes there are still some things to say about this picture.Title: I dont think the title adds something to this photo. I am to lazy to come up with something better now, but its long and doeas not realy tell you anything more. Composition: Good, you didnt crop, this is what came out of your camera, but maybe, just maybe with a little wider shot, this could be even better. I guess you tried that, and you have lots of pictures of this same bird on your hard disk, and this was the best one, but I would still like to see just  a bit more maybe As you already said yourself, the other flamingo could have been cloned out, and it would have made the beautiful contrast with the black background even more perfect, but I dont find it really distracting. Again, its a beautiful picture, and if I where you I would put it up for print, or at least hang it on your own wall. If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me.  Grrrtzzz  Peter', '2004-09-17 17:47:43.000000', '2004-09-17 17:48:09.000000', 0),
(914929, 103063, 22781, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club Comment:</b> <br/> <br/>Hello there.<br/> <br/>What am I looking at here? Wow, again a photo from Iceland.<br/>You must have quite a lot of good photographers in Iceland, because I see more and more of you.<br/>This is again a beautiful photo from Iceland.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your highest score this far, and on your first 6+ photo.<br/> <br/>Some people have complained about the top of the church being cut of. Ive taken a look at your other image in your portfolio, and I must say, even if I dont like the tight crop that much, it makes this one stronger, and it gives the church a bigger feeling, it lets us guess how big it really is.<br/>The floodlight works great on this church and creates beautiful shadows and highlights.<br/>This could have been in a travel guide to Reykjavik, so I believe you succeeded with your photo.<br/> <br/>There is just one thing that I dont like about this photo, and thats the perspective distortion. It looks like the tower is falling. This is a common thing when shooting high buildings especially with wide angle lenses.<br/>There is also a way to correct that with PS.<br/>Just take a look <a href="//www.peachpit.com/articles/article.asp?p=32082&amp;seqNum=9" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a> if you are interested, maybe you can practice on your photo and upload it to your profile when its done, I''m very interested what it will look like then.<br/> <br/>Beautiful picture all in all. <br/> <br/>If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me. <br/> <br/>Grrrtzzz <br/> <br/>Peter<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Comment:  Hello there. What am I looking at here? Wow, again a photo from Iceland.You must have quite a lot of good photographers in Iceland, because I see more and more of you.This is again a beautiful photo from Iceland. Congratulations on your highest score this far, and on your first 6+ photo. Some people have complained about the top of the church being cut of. Ive taken a look at your other image in your portfolio, and I must say, even if I dont like the tight crop that much, it makes this one stronger, and it gives the church a bigger feeling, it lets us guess how big it really is.The floodlight works great on this church and creates beautiful shadows and highlights.This could have been in a travel guide to Reykjavik, so I believe you succeeded with your photo. There is just one thing that I dont like about this photo, and thats the perspective distortion. It looks like the tower is falling. This is a common thing when shooting high buildings especially with wide angle lenses.There is also a way to correct that with PS.Just take a look here if you are interested, maybe you can practice on your photo and upload it to your profile when its done, I''m very interested what it will look like then. Beautiful picture all in all.  If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me.  Grrrtzzz  Peter', '2004-09-17 19:33:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(915156, 102741, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>Hi Philos31...<br/> <br/>I don''t believe this photo needs much ''critique''.  I can''t suggest any real improvements in it without suggesting shooting at some different times on different days looking for the best possible sky for a background.  Excellent shot :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... Hi Philos31... I don''t believe this photo needs much ''critique''.  I can''t suggest any real improvements in it without suggesting shooting at some different times on different days looking for the best possible sky for a background.  Excellent shot :) John Setzler', '2004-09-17 22:37:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(915329, 101611, 3697, '<td valign="top">Thanks for that great critique Philos :)</td>', 'Thanks for that great critique Philos :)', '2004-09-18 00:33:27.000000', NULL, 0),
