(915559, 102741, 22781, '<td valign="top">Thanx John,<br/> <br/>It was the end of summer here in Holland, one of the last few warm day''s and as this is a 2 hour drive I had to take this photo and use it.<br/>I know the sky is boring, and could do with some clouds and maybe some extra color, but I''m still happy with my 16th place.</td>', 'Thanx John, It was the end of summer here in Holland, one of the last few warm day''s and as this is a 2 hour drive I had to take this photo and use it.I know the sky is boring, and could do with some clouds and maybe some extra color, but I''m still happy with my 16th place.', '2004-09-18 05:59:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(915733, 102350, 16219, '<td valign="top">Very Nice, good work in spotting this scene and in your editing as well. I wonder how it would look with a darker sky rather than light, contrasting the trees and complying more with the hues of the water yet excentuating the bridge. As an uneditied photo i am sure this one came as close to perfection as any.</td>', 'Very Nice, good work in spotting this scene and in your editing as well. I wonder how it would look with a darker sky rather than light, contrasting the trees and complying more with the hues of the water yet excentuating the bridge. As an uneditied photo i am sure this one came as close to perfection as any.', '2004-09-18 11:45:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(915829, 103255, 11793, '<td valign="top">well done - and congratulations on a high finish</td>', 'well done - and congratulations on a high finish', '2004-09-18 14:11:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(915893, 102899, 22781, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club Comment:</b> <br/> <br/>Hello there.<br/> <br/>Another photo that will be difficult to critique.<br/>Trust me, it isnt easy with so many good shots in this challenge.<br/>And there''s not much more to add to the comments you allready recieved.<br/>From the comments I filtered a few, one says there is too much rock, the other says he likes the rocks.<br/>I myself think they give more perspective so I say I like the rocks.<br/> <br/>I think you had to score a bit higher with this photo, but the competition was really tough this time (I know, I entered) so be happy with your photo and the place it ended. It shows you have an eye for good compositions.<br/> <br/>If you ask me, why it scored lower then some others, I can only say this. <br/>Its really a photo that would go into a travel guide, but it doesnt show anything really exiting. Its rocks and water. And I think that would be the reason why it didnt score better.<br/> <br/>I say it again, I think this is a good picture, there is nothing that you must improve (well maybe the sky a bit) but the subject is just not as exiting as some other photos in this challenge.<br/> <br/>I took the liberty to visit your profile and found another photo that I really liked, I gave a comment on that too.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work. <br/> <br/>Grrrrtttzzzz<br/> <br/>Peter/CC<br/> <br/>If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me. <br/></td>', 'Critique Club Comment:  Hello there. Another photo that will be difficult to critique.Trust me, it isnt easy with so many good shots in this challenge.And there''s not much more to add to the comments you allready recieved.From the comments I filtered a few, one says there is too much rock, the other says he likes the rocks.I myself think they give more perspective so I say I like the rocks. I think you had to score a bit higher with this photo, but the competition was really tough this time (I know, I entered) so be happy with your photo and the place it ended. It shows you have an eye for good compositions. If you ask me, why it scored lower then some others, I can only say this. Its really a photo that would go into a travel guide, but it doesnt show anything really exiting. Its rocks and water. And I think that would be the reason why it didnt score better. I say it again, I think this is a good picture, there is nothing that you must improve (well maybe the sky a bit) but the subject is just not as exiting as some other photos in this challenge. I took the liberty to visit your profile and found another photo that I really liked, I gave a comment on that too. Keep up the good work.  Grrrrtttzzzz Peter/CC If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me. ', '2004-09-18 15:39:21.000000', NULL, 0),
