(916288, 101995, 26332, '<td valign="top">This picture is pretty incredible. I love it.</td>', 'This picture is pretty incredible. I love it.', '2004-09-19 03:44:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(916505, 102703, 14089, '<td valign="top"><b><i>Greetings from the Critique Club</i></b> <br/> <br/><b>composition</b> <br/><i>I would like to see this shot with a closer view to capture some of the details in the plant life, and place less emphasis on the negative space that the sky creates. My suggestion is to move further left from where you were standing so you can shoot around the big street light and eliminate it from your composition.  This will help the photo focus more on the tree, bridge, person and fountain.</i> <br/> <br/><b>color</b> <br/><i>The colors in this photograph are my favorite thing about it.  I might however try playing with the saturation in photoshop a bit to bring them out even more.  What would this shot look like if it were taken at dawn or dusk when the sky could also add to the unique coloration of the photo? </i> <br/> <br/><b>contrast</b> <br/><i>Nice contrast is captured with the orange coloration of the trees and fountain lights and the blue of the fountain. </i> <br/> <br/><b>focus</b> <br/><i>I wish it was a bit more crisp, a difficult task at night, but it can be achieved with the use of external flash or alternate lighting sources. (see lighting for my suggestions) </i> <br/> <br/><b>depth of field</b> <br/><i>The DoF here gives the photo a snapshot feel. </i> <br/> <br/><b>lighting</b> <br/><i>Again, try shooting this shot when the sun is just about to rise, or just after it has set for the evening.  This will help you do away with the bluriness, and add soothing colors to the sky background. </i> <br/> <br/><b>any other element of the photo that stands out or is lacking in some way</b> <br/><i>All together this photo is good, I love the location, and it certainly would draw my attention if I saw it in a travel guide.  Please do away with the frame. I don''t see how it adds to the composition/design of the photo, and if you are set on having a frame it is more visually appealling if there is slightly more frame on the bottom than on the top (even as little as one pixel) </i> <br/> <br/>Hope this helps! Let me know if you need any clarifications. ~Rob</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  composition I would like to see this shot with a closer view to capture some of the details in the plant life, and place less emphasis on the negative space that the sky creates. My suggestion is to move further left from where you were standing so you can shoot around the big street light and eliminate it from your composition.  This will help the photo focus more on the tree, bridge, person and fountain.  color The colors in this photograph are my favorite thing about it.  I might however try playing with the saturation in photoshop a bit to bring them out even more.  What would this shot look like if it were taken at dawn or dusk when the sky could also add to the unique coloration of the photo?   contrast Nice contrast is captured with the orange coloration of the trees and fountain lights and the blue of the fountain.   focus I wish it was a bit more crisp, a difficult task at night, but it can be achieved with the use of external flash or alternate lighting sources. (see lighting for my suggestions)   depth of field The DoF here gives the photo a snapshot feel.   lighting Again, try shooting this shot when the sun is just about to rise, or just after it has set for the evening.  This will help you do away with the bluriness, and add soothing colors to the sky background.   any other element of the photo that stands out or is lacking in some way All together this photo is good, I love the location, and it certainly would draw my attention if I saw it in a travel guide.  Please do away with the frame. I don''t see how it adds to the composition/design of the photo, and if you are set on having a frame it is more visually appealling if there is slightly more frame on the bottom than on the top (even as little as one pixel)   Hope this helps! Let me know if you need any clarifications. ~Rob', '2004-09-19 14:56:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(916576, 103086, 22781, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club Comment:</b> <br/> <br/>Hi Tom.<br/> <br/>Great picture, like most of your work. Lighting, subject, color, sharpness. Everything spot on. <br/>Im even a bit jealous, about the photo, and about the game, and that was what this challenge was about, make people want to go there. <br/>And that was what you did. There is not much really I can add to the comments you''ve already received, saying that there is not much to criticize about at all. <br/>Theres just one thing missing, its not available as print<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work. <br/> <br/>If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me. <br/> <br/>Grrrtzzz <br/> <br/>Peter<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Comment:  Hi Tom. Great picture, like most of your work. Lighting, subject, color, sharpness. Everything spot on. Im even a bit jealous, about the photo, and about the game, and that was what this challenge was about, make people want to go there. And that was what you did. There is not much really I can add to the comments you''ve already received, saying that there is not much to criticize about at all. Theres just one thing missing, its not available as print Keep up the good work.  If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me.  Grrrtzzz  Peter', '2004-09-19 16:28:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(916594, 102808, 22781, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club Comment:</b> <br/> <br/>Hi there,<br/> <br/>The imperial Palace in China. Hmmm the title makes me want to go there (I love Asia). Looking at this picture doesnt really help that, and that was the meaning of this challenge.<br/>Take a picture that would go in a travel guide. Even though youve made an interesting photo, you scored low (lowest personal scoring ever as far as I have seen). Its not because its a bad photo, but its because the voter doesnt see it in a travel guide.<br/>I think if you had taken a photo of the palace itself, with a bit less sky, it would score much higher.<br/>Take a look at the highest scoring photos watch what they did and how they scored.<br/>As much as I love negative space, I just think it didnt work really well for this photo, the sky is just not interesting enough. If you had used some kind of filter (Gradual ND, or color filter), or waited for sunset maybe it would have worked better, but now its just pure sky. <br/>Youve voted yourself, so you know how it is, a picture comes up, you look, press a number and the next one comes up. 1 or 2 seconds per photo, only stopping for the WOWs.<br/>If people dont see what they expect they vote low, if they dont know what you are trying to say, they vote low. And you see the result, a good photo, but a bad score.<br/>Keep in mind that we are a community with lots of different people and you have to keep your photos easy and understandable.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work. <br/> <br/>If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me. <br/> <br/>Grrrtzzz <br/> <br/>Peter<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Comment:  Hi there, The imperial Palace in China. Hmmm the title makes me want to go there (I love Asia). Looking at this picture doesnt really help that, and that was the meaning of this challenge.Take a picture that would go in a travel guide. Even though youve made an interesting photo, you scored low (lowest personal scoring ever as far as I have seen). Its not because its a bad photo, but its because the voter doesnt see it in a travel guide.I think if you had taken a photo of the palace itself, with a bit less sky, it would score much higher.Take a look at the highest scoring photos watch what they did and how they scored.As much as I love negative space, I just think it didnt work really well for this photo, the sky is just not interesting enough. If you had used some kind of filter (Gradual ND, or color filter), or waited for sunset maybe it would have worked better, but now its just pure sky. Youve voted yourself, so you know how it is, a picture comes up, you look, press a number and the next one comes up. 1 or 2 seconds per photo, only stopping for the WOWs.If people dont see what they expect they vote low, if they dont know what you are trying to say, they vote low. And you see the result, a good photo, but a bad score.Keep in mind that we are a community with lots of different people and you have to keep your photos easy and understandable. Keep up the good work.  If you have any questions, comments or other things about this critique, or are bored and want to spam someone just PM me.  Grrrtzzz  Peter', '2004-09-19 16:59:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(916664, 103006, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/>Overall a pleasing photo.  The patch of sky in the upper right does pull the eye away from the subject a bit.  Perhaps a bit mor brightness also could have helped.  The darkness of the bushes at the left of the arch also detracts a bit.  All in all, the picture does make me want to go see this place.  Well done.</td>', 'Critique Club Review:Overall a pleasing photo.  The patch of sky in the upper right does pull the eye away from the subject a bit.  Perhaps a bit mor brightness also could have helped.  The darkness of the bushes at the left of the arch also detracts a bit.  All in all, the picture does make me want to go see this place.  Well done.', '2004-09-19 18:02:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(916694, 102350, 10626, '<td valign="top">I just can say:<br/> <br/>Well deserved it ! :D <br/>COngratulations</td>', 'I just can say: Well deserved it ! :D COngratulations', '2004-09-19 18:58:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(916861, 103053, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Composition is good, but colors run cool.  The heaviness of the blue makes the picture look cold.  First thing that comes to mind is that it is too cold to swim today.  This almost looks like it could be a beach in Alaska.  The darkness of the picture almost renders the chair as an outline.<br/> <br/>Depth of field is good also.  Did you use zoom?  Things look a little compressed as if a higher level of zoom was used.<br/> <br/>Overall a good picture and with some editing for color and brightness it could be very good.  All the basic structures are there.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: Composition is good, but colors run cool.  The heaviness of the blue makes the picture look cold.  First thing that comes to mind is that it is too cold to swim today.  This almost looks like it could be a beach in Alaska.  The darkness of the picture almost renders the chair as an outline. Depth of field is good also.  Did you use zoom?  Things look a little compressed as if a higher level of zoom was used. Overall a good picture and with some editing for color and brightness it could be very good.  All the basic structures are there.', '2004-09-19 22:04:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(916874, 103236, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Overall I really like this picture, so I''ll have to nitpick here.<br/>Perspective is a smidge off.  Either the camera was a tiny bit off level, or there is some distortion from the lens.  The buildings on the left should be absolutely vertical.  The taller the building the more telling it is.  The key to this shot is the reflections.  Including all of the buildings would have made it even better.  (Perhaps it wasn''t possbile from available vantage points, but it is something to keep in mind.) I also might have cropped the bit of light colored building at the bitter left edge of the picture.  Finishing the left edge of the building in shadow really works here, and the bit of brightness doesn''t add anything.<br/> <br/>Color and saturation is very good. Reminds me of a Kodachrome(tm) slide.  The buildings are the tiniest bit soft, but at 640x480 there can only be so much sharpness.  <br/> <br/>As I said at the opening, I really like this picture.  It makes me want to see it in person, which was the object of the challenge. Well done!</td>', 'Critique Club Review: Overall I really like this picture, so I''ll have to nitpick here.Perspective is a smidge off.  Either the camera was a tiny bit off level, or there is some distortion from the lens.  The buildings on the left should be absolutely vertical.  The taller the building the more telling it is.  The key to this shot is the reflections.  Including all of the buildings would have made it even better.  (Perhaps it wasn''t possbile from available vantage points, but it is something to keep in mind.) I also might have cropped the bit of light colored building at the bitter left edge of the picture.  Finishing the left edge of the building in shadow really works here, and the bit of brightness doesn''t add anything. Color and saturation is very good. Reminds me of a Kodachrome(tm) slide.  The buildings are the tiniest bit soft, but at 640x480 there can only be so much sharpness.   As I said at the opening, I really like this picture.  It makes me want to see it in person, which was the object of the challenge. Well done!', '2004-09-19 22:16:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(916882, 102859, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>The trouble with framing is that sometimes there can be too much of a good thing.  The foliage on the right works well.  The brightness of the left competes, and the center obscures the building.  The depth of field falls short, as the camera has focused on the foliage at the fence leaving the building a bit soft.  It should be the other way round.  The upper fence rails at first appear as if they were part of the building due to this effect.<br/> <br/>Color and saturation are good.  A bit of editing could punch up the coulds in the sky to add more drama to this picture.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: The trouble with framing is that sometimes there can be too much of a good thing.  The foliage on the right works well.  The brightness of the left competes, and the center obscures the building.  The depth of field falls short, as the camera has focused on the foliage at the fence leaving the building a bit soft.  It should be the other way round.  The upper fence rails at first appear as if they were part of the building due to this effect. Color and saturation are good.  A bit of editing could punch up the coulds in the sky to add more drama to this picture.', '2004-09-19 22:24:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(916889, 102797, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>What would have helped here is a pocket level.  Small levels that you can place on the camera to make sure that the horizion is level.  Here the picture slopes from left to right.<br/> <br/>The editing has left the coulds blown out at the whitest parts on the left side of the frame.  Yet the rest of the frame works quite well, as this reminds me of a 50''s travel brochure, the way the colors and lighting are on the grass and people.  (I love those old photos.)<br/> <br/>Overall a very good picture, and well meets the challenge as it makes me want to come see it in person also.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: What would have helped here is a pocket level.  Small levels that you can place on the camera to make sure that the horizion is level.  Here the picture slopes from left to right. The editing has left the coulds blown out at the whitest parts on the left side of the frame.  Yet the rest of the frame works quite well, as this reminds me of a 50''s travel brochure, the way the colors and lighting are on the grass and people.  (I love those old photos.) Overall a very good picture, and well meets the challenge as it makes me want to come see it in person also.', '2004-09-19 22:30:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(918206, 103081, 24495, '<td valign="top">Wonderful Shot!</td>', 'Wonderful Shot!', '2004-09-20 13:38:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(919016, 102808, 11050, '<td valign="top">This photograph has very strong graphical elements and is fairly well balanced and definitely does not deserve such score. <br/> <br/>My eyes are immediately drawn to the slightly lit roof. Excellent touch. <br/> <br/>The silhouette adds to the mystery to the scene, which makes me want to look deeper in the photograph. <br/> <br/>The dramatic sky, which some may argue to be a distraction, imho actually serves to give the context "Heavenly Palace."<br/> <br/>A very unconventional and interesting photo. If I had voted, probably a 7 because it is so different from everyone else.<br/> <br/>Cheers, William</td>', 'This photograph has very strong graphical elements and is fairly well balanced and definitely does not deserve such score.  My eyes are immediately drawn to the slightly lit roof. Excellent touch.  The silhouette adds to the mystery to the scene, which makes me want to look deeper in the photograph.  The dramatic sky, which some may argue to be a distraction, imho actually serves to give the context "Heavenly Palace." A very unconventional and interesting photo. If I had voted, probably a 7 because it is so different from everyone else. Cheers, William', '2004-09-21 04:52:11.000000', NULL, 0),
